{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792952653,"nonce":"/Ok9pN9508mLqzZ94MGEa1PsUY8=","message":"Native effect and blend owners now join eligible native, plain/styled text, SVG and image descendants across BG/FG streams. Color/spatial effects and non-normal blends request capture even at opacity one when collected content needs the group. Unsupported moving or effect owners discard nested capture candidates and retain their fallback. The existing motion/collected-content resolver, opacity commands, clip ownership, image texture handles, raster pixels, geometry rebasing and ordered compositor are reused. Glass/material boundaries, 3D, global overlays, flow/custom GPU passes, named Sample and legacy collection remain separate.\n\nNative mask resources are preloaded after deferred content resolves, in static and dynamic batches and both BG/FG command streams. Loading a real mask exposed an existing GPU upload mismatch: MaskImageUniforms supplied 16 bytes while the unchanged WGSL uniform structure requires 32 due to its aligned vec3 padding. Its CPU padding and upload initializer now supply 32 bytes. Public Rust MaskImageUniforms._pad is seven floats; shader code, GPU primitive/image instance layouts and shared ClipPath ABI are unchanged.\n\nNegative image pixel (30,30) was [0,160,96,255], expected native isolated/color-swapped [64,64,128,255]. The first expanded run passed six cases and exposed the mask validation failure plus an invalid reference assumption for motion bindings. Motion builders add an outer opacity wrapper; the corrected oracle retains that boundary instead of moving opacity onto the inner blend owner. No blend-kernel change was needed. An initial fixture image-module name collision was corrected before pixel checks.\n\nTen new cases cover all native LayerEffect variants (color matrix, blur, drop shadow, glow, image masks in alpha and luminance modes), chained effects/blending, Multiply/Screen/Difference, direct/compositor, BG/FG owners, mixed plain/styled text/SVG/image/RGBA order, authored alpha and later siblings, effect replacement/removal, opacity zero/one recovery and replay for static/binding/both CSS stores, nested effects, affine/path clips, DPI and expanded/cropped bounds. Complete frames compare to an independently prepared native group with the same existing effect compositor. CPU controls cover missing resolver capabilities, native-only groups without collected capabilities, unsupported flow/global overlay/glass/3D boundaries, and nested native fallback beneath an unsupported effect owner.\n\nCosts: more eligible layers retain prepared content and may require larger pooled targets to include foreground/text/image bounds and blur/shadow/glow expansion. Existing straightening/effect intermediates and non-normal blend destination snapshots are reused; blend sampling retains the existing target COPY_SRC requirement. Newly referenced image masks decode/upload once per distinct URI into the existing renderer mask cache, retaining that cache's lifetime policy. CPU mask uploads add 16 bytes. Missing/moving content retains conservative repaint behavior; no new target/cache system, effect algorithm or timing/memory benchmark. No browser/mobile pixel or performance claim.\n\nFinal scoped counts and commit SHA are in the completion comment. Logs /private/tmp/blinc-effect-group-{negative,first,binding,final-normal,text,styled,svg,image,cross,opacity,foreground,scratch,producer,overlay,dt-effect_group}.log. Drivers /private/tmp/blinc_effect_group_gates.py and /private/tmp/blinc_effect_group_modes.py. Jobs=2, capacities 1024, offscreen only, no source edits during builds. No broad workspace/DSL/docs/platform gates or pushes.\n\nParent e0a7502 remains open for unsupported mixed/global overlay/glass/3D owners, custom GPU passes/meshes, named Sample and legacy render_tree collection. Secondary-window isolation 3d90a31 remains separate.","files":null}]}